as we continue to fight the pandemic  many are still dealing with health  issues and job loss  though we are slowly recovering many are  still dealing with depression or  addiction  after such a hard year since april is  alcohol awareness month bianca holman  shares the story of one former nfl  player  who overcame his alcoholic addiction  i would say addiction she is a beautiful  mistress but she will take it all from  you she's a very jealous lover patrick  vinsky is at desert hope addiction  treatment center  his affair with alcohol began in 2008  the housing market crash hit him hard  he went from being a multi-millionaire  realtor to living on food stamps in  order to support his family  i could tell i used alcohol just like a  tool like i used painkillers in the nfl  i struggle to function one more day  i didn't care about my long-term health  i just want to make it through one more  day so i can feed my kids  vinsky fights the misconception daily  about addiction being a  lack of self-control he was a gladiator  on the field for years  the first german citizen playing for  three nfl teams  the jaguars eagles and colts  binsky went from a casual drink enjoying  a nice glass of red wine with a steak  to something more oh you got the shakes  in the morning and you think maybe a  little white thought to watch the  sunrise would be great  and then by lunch you're like maybe 12  pack in you know  and you you don't feel like you're drunk  anything you just try to normalize  your feelings as vinsky finishes his  program at desert hope  he's five months sober and wants to  dedicate his life to helping others  i gotta call it big man or a van a big  man in a van and it's gonna be broadcast  and i wanna go through the united states  talking to high schools  sharing the message that it may start  and fun but sometimes addiction  may end in death bianca holman 8 news  now
 

